# Stripe. Copy to .env for local work. Never commit a filled in copy.
#
# In production these live in Vercel: Settings -> Environment Variables.
# Full explanation in STRIPE-SETUP.md.

# Server only. NEVER prefix this with VITE_. Anything named VITE_something is
# bundled into the JavaScript every visitor downloads, and a leaked secret key
# means somebody else can charge your customers and read your data.
#
# Vercel: the live sk_live_... on Production ONLY, and the sandbox sk_test_...
# on Preview and Development. That split is what stops a preview deploy
# charging a real card.
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...

# Server only. The webhook signing secret, used to prove an incoming event
# really came from Stripe.
#
# This takes a COMMA SEPARATED LIST. Put both the live secret and the sandbox
# one here, on Production only:
#
#   STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_theLiveOne,whsec_theSandboxOne
#
# Both accounts send to the same live URL, and the handler tries each secret in
# turn. It only ever verifies and emails, so it holds no secret key and does
# not care which account an event came from. A sandbox event arrives labelled
# [TEST]. Preview builds never receive a webhook and do not need this at all.
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...

# The public origin, used to build the URL Stripe returns the buyer to.
#
# Set this on Production ONLY. api/checkout.ts falls back to the host the
# request arrived on, so a preview deploy returns the buyer to that preview
# rather than bouncing them to the live site in the middle of a test.
SITE_URL=https://www.calpir.com

# Where webhook notifications are emailed. Optional: defaults to the same
# Formspree endpoint the contact form uses.
# NOTIFY_FORM_ENDPOINT=https://formspree.io/f/...
